0..79 Comment "//! Atom sorts follow [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]"
80..128 Comment "//! and [Gabbay-2009-nominal_universal_algebra]."
129..132 Comment "//!"
133..209 Comment "//! An `Atom` sort is orbit-infinite. Equality and swapping provide its only"
210..224 Comment "//! structure."
225..228 Comment "//!"
229..287 Comment "//! Operations take atoms. Operations do not return atoms."
288..368 Comment "//! Each block is a `Theory` value. Its sort chain has an `Atom` link. A program"
369..398 Comment "//! reads the link by `case`."
399..402 Comment "//!"
403..473 Comment "//! - cites: [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]"
474..526 Comment "//! - cites: [Gabbay-2009-nominal_universal_algebra]"
527..530 Comment "//!"
531..696 Comment "//! [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]: https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139084673 \"Pitts, Nominal Sets: Names and Symmetry in Computer Science\""
697..873 Comment "//! [Gabbay-2009-nominal_universal_algebra]: https://doi.org/10.1093/logcom/exp033 \"Gabbay and Mathijssen, Nominal (Universal) Algebra: Equational Logic with Names and Binding\""
